---
layout: base.njk
pagination:
  data: packages
  size: 1
  alias: pkg
permalink: "/packages/{{ pkg.dirName }}/"
eleventyComputed:
  title: "{{ pkg.name }}"
---

<h1>{{ pkg.name }} <small>v{{ pkg.version }}</small></h1>
<p>{{ pkg.description }}</p>
<p><a href="{{ ('/storybooks/' + pkg.dirName + '/') | url }}">View Storybook →</a></p>

<h2>Install</h2>
<p>
  This package is distributed privately. It is not on public npm. Pick one of
  the two options below.
</p>

<h3>Option 1: private registry</h3>
<p>
  Requires a registry token. Ask the maintainer for one, then add this to your
  project's <code>.npmrc</code> and export the token as <code>NPM_TOKEN</code>:
</p>
<pre><code>@tkottke90:registry={{ site.registryUrl }}
//{{ site.registryHost }}/:_authToken=${NPM_TOKEN}</code></pre>
<pre><code>npm install {{ pkg.name }}</code></pre>

<h3>Option 2: download the tarball</h3>
<p>
  <a href="{{ pkg.releaseUrl }}">Download {{ pkg.tarballName }}</a>
  (from the <a href="{{ site.repoUrl }}/releases/tag/v{{ pkg.version }}">v{{ pkg.version }} release</a>).
  Then either install it directly:
</p>
<pre><code>npm install ./{{ pkg.tarballName }}</code></pre>
<p>or unpack it into <code>node_modules</code> yourself:</p>
<pre><code>mkdir -p node_modules/{{ pkg.name }}
tar -xzf {{ pkg.tarballName }} -C node_modules/{{ pkg.name }} --strip-components=1</code></pre>
<p>
  Manual unpacking skips dependency installation. If the package lists
  dependencies, run <code>npm install</code> in your project afterwards.
</p>
